# API URL for the backend (optional, defaults to /qa/v1)
# VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8080/qa/v1

# --- OIDC (Phase C, Task 15) -------------------------------------------------
# Both are optional: src/auth/provider.tsx defaults them to the values below,
# which are what a local development stack serves.
# vite inlines import.meta.env at BUILD time, and the UI image is built from a
# context that carries no .env, so an override has to be supplied as a docker
# build arg (deploy/docker/qa-platform-ui.Dockerfile declares both) or by
# creating a .env here before `npm run build`.
#
# THE ISSUER IS THE BROWSER'S URL, not the gears'. It is also the `iss` claim
# Keycloak stamps into the token. `https://keycloak:8443/realms/qa-platform` is
# the gears' discovery URL -- it resolves only inside the cluster and is pinned
# to a private CA, so it must NEVER appear in a VITE_ variable.
# VITE_OIDC_ISSUER=http://localhost:8180/realms/qa-platform
#
# The realm's public client: publicClient=true, standardFlowEnabled=true,
# pkce.code.challenge.method=S256, redirectUris=["http://localhost:8080/*"]
# (deploy/helm/qa-platform/files/keycloak/realm-qa-platform.json).
# VITE_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=qa-platform-ui
